  "configuration_id": "config_015",
  "reason": "1) Evidence/uncertainty: We know resnet50 image-only (single profile) is very weak (acc=0.208), and that ViT-L in the multimodal setting boosts performance from ~0.69 (resnet50) to ~0.72. However, we have zero data on whether ViT-L captures any standalone cellular phenotype signal. The image modality's role—purely complementary vs. having independent predictive power—remains untested. 2) What this tests: config_015 (image_only, multiprofile, ViT-L, transformer) isolates the image modality with the best available encoder and matching multiprofile/transformer settings, directly measuring ViT-L's standalone contribution. 3) Why it is the best next experiment: Under a limited budget, this clean ablation is highly informative. If image-only ViT-L remains near 0.2–0.3, it confirms the image is purely complementary and future effort should focus on RNA-image interaction/fusion. If it reaches ~0.5+, the image has strong standalone signal and we should invest in image pipeline improvements. This single result fundamentally reshapes where to allocate remaining experiments, making it more decision-relevant than marginal fusion or aggregation tweaks that are already well-characterized."
}

